<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raymond VI, Count of Toulouse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1156–<a href="/years/1222">1222</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raymond VI was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> from 1194 to 1222. Accused of protecting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catharism">Cathars</a>, he was excommunicated, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a> from 1209 brought northern French armies under Simon de Montfort into his lands. He was defeated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-ii-of-aragon">Peter II of Aragon</a> at Muret in 1213 and lost Toulouse, but recovered it in 1217 and held it until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raymond-vi-count-of-toulouse.jpg" alt="Raymond VI, Count of Toulouse" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raimond6Toulouse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
